Initial sync of a declarative binding: `text(value=name)` with name = "World"
must produce a span whose textContent the script seeds on load, without any
user interaction.

The generated script holds one state object carrying the var's initial value,
a single __sngl_init() containing the inlined DOM write, and a call to it at
the bottom of the script. A binding that is only ever initialised no longer
gets a per-prop updater function of its own:

deny out/none/html/index.html `\$u__n0_text` -- an init-only binding has no per-prop updater; its write is inlined into __sngl_init

-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

output { none { html } }

component main node {
    var name = "World"
    text(value=name)
}

window {
    main
}
-- out/none/html/index.html --
